      "Signal 2 — Longevity + Lung Regeneration + Young-vs-Aged scRNA-seq + IPF-Aging-Bridge / Single-cell RNA-seq of Lung Regeneration in Young and Aged Mice After Injury [lung-regeneration aging-bridge scRNA-seq atlas]: GSE303646 (score 4, n=56, Mus musculus, Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing [single-cell RNA-seq], pdat 2026/09/15 = 3 days ago, raw TXT files, raw_file_availability 'yes', watcher query 'lung fibrosis single-cell') is the FRESHEST NOVEL lung-regeneration / young-vs-aged / single-cell-RNA-seq / injury-repair atlas in the entire 2026-09-18 hits.jsonl. It is a direct longevity + bioinformatics + lung-regeneration + aging-fibroblast-vulnerability + senescent-cell-burden input for the BB longevity + bioinformatics + multiomics lane, distinct from Signal 1 AP-1-companion-bundle by deliverable (young-vs-aged-regeneration-time-series vs master-regulator-perturbation), and from yesterday's id:99 GSE345643 pressure-loaded-RV multimodal atlas by tissue (lung-vs-right-ventricle). Lung regeneration declines steeply with age — young-mice can fully regenerate AT2-alveolar-type-2-cell populations after naphthalene-injury within ~14 days, while aged-mice show persistent-inflammation, failed-AT2-regeneration, and progression-to-fibrosis. The dataset's n=56 sample-count (sufficient for young-vs-aged-clustering + injury-vs-uninjured-clustering + cell-type-stratified-fibroblast-state-analysis + AT2-vs-AT1-lineage-trajectory + senescent-cell-abundance-quantification + SASP-cytokine-scoring) makes it an ideal training-set for AI-DD lung-regeneration-foundation-models and IPF-aging-bridge-stratification-models. The senescent-fibroblast burden in aged lungs (CDKN2A/p16INK4a+, CDKN1A/p21CIP1+, SASP-IL-6+, IL-1beta+, CXCL1+) is a key predictor of failed-regeneration and progression-to-fibrosis.",
